meta {
  name: Create POSTGIS DataSink
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/datasinks
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{dataSetId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "dataSinkType": "POSTGIS",
    "configuration": {
      "tableName": "sensor_observations",
      "dataStructureVersionId": "{{dataStructureVersionId}}"
    }
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.body && res.body.id) {
    bru.setVar('dataSinkId', res.body.id);
    bru.setVar('postgisDataSinkId', res.body.id);
  }
}

docs {
  **Precondition:** `dataSetId` and `dataStructureVersionId` are set. The setup folder seeds the DataSet but not a version — run `datastructures/create-version.bru` first (or set `dataStructureVersionId` manually) to populate that variable.

  **Expected Response:** 201 Created, body contains `id` and the resolved configuration (with an inline DataStructureVersion summary).

  **Post-condition:** Save `dataSinkId` and `postgisDataSinkId` from `body.id`. `postgisDataSinkId` is the sticky reference used by `layers/create-layer.bru` and `pipelines/attach-datasinks-to-pipeline.bru`.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | DataSink record created in `portal_backend` DB, linked to the DataSet |
  | Config Adapter | — (the GeoServer workspace/datastore is provisioned when the parent DataSet is released) |
  | External System | — |
}
